# Per-VM tenant host list — copy to deploy/tenants.caddy (gitignored; deploy.sh
# does this automatically if the file is missing) and add one block per tenant
# subdomain. Each host also needs a DNS A record pointing at this VM.
#
# After editing, apply without downtime:
#   ./compose.sh exec caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
# Caddy mounts this single file, so the container keeps the inode it started
# with: an editor that saves by writing a new file and renaming it over this one
# leaves Caddy reading the old list and the reload silently changes nothing. Edit
# in place, or recreate instead: ./compose.sh up -d --no-deps --force-recreate caddy
# (add-tenant.sh, remove-tenant.sh and deploy.sh check for this themselves).
#
# Example — the `acme` tenant on feohledger.com:
#
# acme.feohledger.com {
# 	import spa
# }
